AuthorDate: Sat Nov 7 19:36:00 2026 +0000
Commit:     Viche Recovery Steward <recovery-steward@viche.local>
CommitDate: Sat Nov 7 19:36:00 2026 +0000

    Publish the archive lock atomically to remove the ownership race
    
    Review found a window where the lock directory existed before its PID was
    written, so a contender could misread it as dead and enter the critical
    section, and two contenders could both reclaim the same dead lock.
    
    Replace the directory lock with a pid FILE published by an atomic hard link:
    it never exists without a holder, so there is no empty-PID window. Reclaim a
    dead holder by renaming the stale lock to a unique name; only the contender
    whose rename succeeds deletes it, so concurrent reclaimers cannot both win.
    A live holder is always respected. Add a two-contender regression that
    archives two different agents from one hold file and asserts neither line is
    lost.

